cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this Lean companion, please cite the software below and the paper
  it formalizes (listed under references). The Lean formalization was carried out
  by Le Chen (with AI assistance as disclosed in the README); Ian Ruau and Wenxian
  Shen are coauthors of the paper.
type: software
title: 'Lean companion to "Chemotaxis models with signal-dependent sensitivity and
  a logistic-type source, III: Bifurcation and spike-like solutions"'
authors:
- family-names: Chen
  given-names: Le
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/chenle02/chemotaxis-paper-iii-lean
url: https://github.com/chenle02/chemotaxis-paper-iii-lean
abstract: 'Partial Lean formalization of Chemotaxis III: finite coefficient/modal
  results, actual stationary estimates and limits, weak-H2 coordinates and complements,
  and conditional bifurcation deductions. Full PDE bifurcation, center manifolds,
  global alternatives and stability are not certified.'
keywords:
- Lean 4
- Mathlib
- formalization
- chemotaxis
- bifurcation
